WEBVTT

00:38.444 --> 00:39.904
God, I hate coming to the vet.

00:40.072 --> 00:42.490
They charge me 90 bucks a day
to keep Brian here.

00:42.657 --> 00:44.867
For 60 bucks, I could
put him up at the Holiday Inn.

00:45.035 --> 00:46.327
Eh? Who's with me?

00:49.163 --> 00:53.751
My apologies, my pet cricket
has restless leg syndrome.

00:53.918 --> 00:57.296
I hope Brian's stomach pains
aren't anything serious.

00:57.463 --> 01:00.050
Look at that, Lois,
that's why cats freak me out.

01:00.216 --> 01:03.636
It's doing that weird stretchy-leg thing
where they lick themselves.

01:06.889 --> 01:09.559
Look at that, huh?
Look at that shit.

01:09.727 --> 01:10.768
Ew.

01:10.935 --> 01:13.688
Oh, thank God the vets are here
to help Brian.

01:13.855 --> 01:15.898
I wanna be a veterinarian
when I grow up.

01:16.065 --> 01:18.985
Meg, we've been over this.
You're gonna gain 150 pounds...

01:19.152 --> 01:20.903
<i>...and write Ugly Betty fan fiction.</i>

01:21.070 --> 01:22.739
- But, Dad...
- Meg, that's final.

01:22.905 --> 01:24.700
Meg, that's final. Meg, that's final.

01:24.867 --> 01:27.034
See, this bird knows
what I'm talking about.

01:27.201 --> 01:29.580
- Thank you. Thank you.
- Thank you. Thank you.

01:29.747 --> 01:31.330
- You're polite.
- You're polite.

01:31.497 --> 01:35.209
You do not see that these days,
you do not see that. I like you.

01:35.376 --> 01:37.253
- I like you.
- Oh, thank God.

01:37.420 --> 01:39.465
You never know
what somebody thinks of you.

01:39.631 --> 01:41.507
I'm glad I made
a good first impression.

01:41.674 --> 01:44.136
- Would you like to be friends?
- Like to be friends.

01:44.303 --> 01:46.262
Oh, God, this is all going so smoothly.

01:46.429 --> 01:48.181
- What's your name? I'm Peter.
- Peter.

01:48.347 --> 01:49.932
No way, that's my name.

01:50.099 --> 01:51.976
You should spend the night
at my house.

01:52.143 --> 01:53.561
Lois, make up the guest room.

01:53.728 --> 01:56.397
Peter, that's someone's pet,
you can't just take it.

01:56.564 --> 01:59.651
Well, maybe
they'd never know it's gone.

02:05.072 --> 02:09.036
- Oh, Brian, I'm so glad you're okay.
- Yes, he's doing fine.

02:09.203 --> 02:12.914
We were able to clear the stomach
obstruction. It was a used diaper.

02:13.080 --> 02:14.541
- Ew.
- Gross.

02:14.707 --> 02:16.584
Oh, ho, ho, yes.

02:16.751 --> 02:18.712
Get off my back.
I thought it was Indian food.

02:18.879 --> 02:21.297
Oh, thank you so much for your help,
Dr. Jewish.

02:21.464 --> 02:25.051
- I thought we were gonna lose him.
- It was my pleasure, Mrs. Griffin.

02:25.218 --> 02:27.386
Go ahead and check out
with my intern Anna.

03:05.174 --> 03:08.595
<i>We return to Busy Business
Lady Whose Life is Missing Something...</i>

03:08.762 --> 03:11.931
...but She Doesn't Realize It
Because She's So Busy with Business.

03:12.098 --> 03:13.767
<i>I cannot make
that business meeting.</i>

03:13.934 --> 03:17.228
<i>I got a different business meeting
at 3, we'll be doing business.</i>

03:17.395 --> 03:20.147
<i>- Wondering if you're free for coffee.
- Oh, no, I can't.</i>

03:20.314 --> 03:22.943
I've got a lunch meeting and
a meeting after lunch. After that...

03:23.110 --> 03:24.193
Shh, shh, shh.

03:24.360 --> 03:26.696
Over the next 90 minutes,
I'd like to show you...

03:26.862 --> 03:30.449
...that all your problems
can be solved by my penis.

03:37.624 --> 03:40.167
Hey, guys. What is going on?

03:40.334 --> 03:43.088
- No way.
- That thing don't bite, do it?

03:43.255 --> 03:46.716
- Guys, say hello to Adrian Beaky.
- Pick a lane, bitch.

03:46.882 --> 03:49.760
Ain't that funny? Heard me
say that on the way over.

03:49.927 --> 03:51.595
I gotta pee,
where's that Snapple bottle?

03:52.973 --> 03:54.724
I had a gay experience at camp.

03:56.100 --> 03:59.103
We had the radio on, and they
were talking about some goofy stuff.

03:59.270 --> 04:00.646
What are you guys drinking?

04:00.813 --> 04:03.941
Peter, you look like a pirate
with that thing on your shoulder.

04:04.108 --> 04:07.154
- A pirate? Oh, cool.
- You should get a pirate name.

04:07.320 --> 04:09.238
- And a peg leg.
- And a hook hand.

04:09.405 --> 04:11.658
You should have sex
with that crossing guard...

04:11.825 --> 04:13.951
...even though
I found out she was 12.

04:14.118 --> 04:16.580
I mean, you should get an eye patch.

04:16.913 --> 04:18.622
Eye patch would be cool.

04:22.586 --> 04:25.129
You know, Brian, if you like my poop
going into your mouth...

04:25.296 --> 04:27.424
...we can just do that.
- Shut up, Stewie.

04:27.674 --> 04:31.051
Mom, can we go back to the vet
and see the pretty vet assistant again?

04:31.218 --> 04:33.804
Well, I guess if Brian gets sick again.

04:33.971 --> 04:36.850
Oh, boy! Hey, Brian, look.

04:37.017 --> 04:39.185
Brian's sick. Mom, get your keys.

04:39.351 --> 04:40.936
Chris, I'm not going to the vet.

04:41.605 --> 04:42.647
Ha, ha.

04:42.814 --> 04:45.524
- There's me wench.
- Peter, what the hell are you doing?

04:45.691 --> 04:48.236
That's Long John Peter to you,
porthole.

04:50.571 --> 04:53.699
Fetch me five tankards of ale
and a leg of mutton for me mateys.

04:56.745 --> 04:57.996
Who are those guys?

04:58.163 --> 05:00.790
Just a few sea dogs
from my fishing boat days.

05:00.957 --> 05:03.334
I don't care, they stink.
Get them out of here.

05:03.501 --> 05:06.171
They stink of good cheer, Lois. Ha-ha.

05:08.130 --> 05:10.299
After we've had our fill
of bread and wine...

05:10.466 --> 05:14.011
...we shall tell tales of other times
we had our fill of bread and wine.

05:14.178 --> 05:18.599
<i>God, this is a more disturbing sight
than Tom Hanks and E.T. In Philadelphia.</i>

05:18.766 --> 05:20.894
Ouch.

05:21.061 --> 05:22.312
There you go. You're good.

05:22.479 --> 05:25.356
- You didn't touch me.
- I don't wanna get AIDS.

05:30.612 --> 05:32.322
Aah! Kristallnacht!

05:32.489 --> 05:36.868
Aha! 'Tis Long John Peter and his
merry men come seeking plunder.

05:37.035 --> 05:39.578
All your Tucks medicated pads
be ours.

05:39.745 --> 05:41.748
Aah! Oh, my God!

05:41.915 --> 05:43.999
Oh, God. What are you do...?

05:44.166 --> 05:48.420
Aha. For no reason, I'm going to fire
this cannon all over your store.

05:53.384 --> 05:55.762
Aha. Terrible pharmacy toys.

05:55.929 --> 05:58.430
We'll see to it
that no child ever receives these...

05:58.597 --> 06:01.726
...as a last-minute gift
hastily bought on the way to the party.

06:06.898 --> 06:10.360
Dear me, it's almost 3:00.
I've got to get this shipment...

06:10.527 --> 06:14.446
...of sugarcane, tobacco and spices
to the harbor before day's end.

06:16.074 --> 06:18.575
That car is coming up awfully fast.

06:18.742 --> 06:21.162
But at least it's flying the British flag.

06:26.626 --> 06:28.335
Oh, no, privateers.

06:28.502 --> 06:31.339
No doubt they're after my sugarcane,
tobacco and spices.

06:31.506 --> 06:35.468
Well, Shelley Boothbishop isn't about
to let you over-egg this pudding.

06:36.803 --> 06:38.053
Ha-ha.

06:48.689 --> 06:50.233
Prepare to be boarded.

06:50.400 --> 06:52.901
You'll never take my cargo.

07:07.249 --> 07:09.377
Load the cannon.

08:06.767 --> 08:08.102
All clear, sir.

08:10.522 --> 08:11.563
Shoot it again!

08:11.730 --> 08:13.274
What? I didn't understand that.

08:13.441 --> 08:15.944
I said, "shoot it again,"
but I said it pirate-like.

08:31.917 --> 08:34.796
Well done, you barnacle-munching
scallywiggers.

08:34.963 --> 08:36.547
Sir, we've got a man down.

08:36.713 --> 08:39.425
Oh, my God, Adrian Beaky,
say something.

08:39.592 --> 08:42.512
Shoot me.

08:42.679 --> 08:45.848
Oh, God. This is my fault. I did this.

08:46.015 --> 08:47.850
I've screwed up worse
than Disney did...

08:48.017 --> 08:50.979
<i>...when they cast Michael J. Fox
in that Zorro remake.</i>

08:51.145 --> 08:53.773
Who was that masked man
who saved us?

08:53.940 --> 08:57.110
I don't know, but he left his insignia.

09:02.949 --> 09:05.910
Give it to me straight, Dr. Jewish.
Is he gonna live?

09:06.076 --> 09:08.121
Mr. Griffin, your parrot is dead.

09:08.288 --> 09:12.000
No!

09:12.166 --> 09:13.960
Did he at least die with dignity?

09:14.127 --> 09:17.005
Well, he convulsed a lot
and fell off the operating table.

09:17.171 --> 09:19.340
Then he flopped around a little
on the floor.

09:19.507 --> 09:23.469
A nurse accidentally stepped on him,
and kicked him into a puddle of urine.

09:23.636 --> 09:27.056
Which must have frightened him.
His bowels released all over himself.

09:27.223 --> 09:31.018
I tried to pick him up, but I got angry
because some of it got on my thumb.

09:31.184 --> 09:33.855
So I threw him against the wall,
that's where he died.

09:34.022 --> 09:35.856
That's the way I wanna go.

09:36.023 --> 09:39.068
- I'm really sorry about your dad's parrot.
- Well, that's okay.

09:39.235 --> 09:42.238
He'll get over it quickly
and move on to another wacky thing.

09:42.405 --> 09:44.073
Lois, whose pipe organ is this?

09:44.240 --> 09:47.869
- My name's Anna.
- I'm Chris.

09:48.036 --> 09:51.414
Sometimes I have to poop
for a long time.

09:51.581 --> 09:52.790
Now you say something.

09:54.334 --> 09:57.211
You're funny, but I bet
a lot of girls tell you that, huh?

09:57.378 --> 10:01.049
Well, the only girl I know is my sister,
and she sucks.

10:01.215 --> 10:05.635
- Oh, I'm sorry to hear that.
- Wow, we're having a conversation.

10:07.347 --> 10:11.642
Listen, I have to get back to work,
but, um, would you maybe...

10:11.809 --> 10:13.853
...wanna go out some time?
- Yes!

10:14.020 --> 10:17.565
- Great. Here's my number.
- Awesome.

10:17.732 --> 10:19.692
Oh, no. I broke the pipe organ.

10:19.859 --> 10:22.153
Hey, look the deed to a cattle ranch.

10:31.954 --> 10:33.706
So, um...

10:34.165 --> 10:36.084
...how do you like working at the vet?

10:36.250 --> 10:38.211
Oh, it is so rewarding.

10:38.377 --> 10:42.465
Ever since I was a little girl
I have loved working with animals.

10:42.632 --> 10:44.550
Did you make it
with one of the dogs?

10:44.717 --> 10:47.970
- What?
- I mean, did you enjoy your appetizer?

10:48.137 --> 10:51.557
- It hasn't come yet.
- Oh, I mean...

10:51.724 --> 10:55.269
...did you ever make it
with one of the dogs? No, stupid!

10:55.436 --> 10:59.065
- Chris, just relax.
- Um, okay.

10:59.232 --> 11:02.485
So, what kind of stuff
do you like to do and junk?

11:02.652 --> 11:04.988
Well, I really enjoy
some of the music...

11:05.154 --> 11:07.365
...black people
have been coming up with lately.

11:09.283 --> 11:11.869
You know, Anna,
when I first saw you...

11:12.036 --> 11:14.539
...I thought you were
the most beautiful girl...

11:14.705 --> 11:17.500
...and now all I wanna do
is show you my innermost self...

11:17.667 --> 11:21.087
...but I'm afraid you'll reject me
because you won't like what you see.

11:21.254 --> 11:23.965
Or that you'll see my scrotum
and see that seam on it...

11:24.131 --> 11:27.051
...then you'll think I'm made up
of two guys sewn together...

11:27.218 --> 11:29.178
...because that's
what I think happened...

11:29.345 --> 11:32.056
Chris, I like you.

11:35.101 --> 11:37.687
- You don't have to try so hard.
- I'm sorry.

11:37.854 --> 11:40.231
When I'm around a pretty girl
I get worked up...

11:40.398 --> 11:42.525
...like a kid
watching a toy commercial.

11:42.692 --> 11:43.985
<i>Kids, kids, kids.</i>

11:44.151 --> 11:46.320
<i>Shiny. Gooey. Stretchy. Fun.</i>

11:46.487 --> 11:47.947
<i>Hasbro's Best Thing Ever.</i>

11:48.114 --> 11:50.324
<i>Sticky. Yummy. Bouncy. Fun.</i>

11:50.491 --> 11:51.909
<i>Hasbro's Best Thing Ever.</i>

11:52.076 --> 11:53.411
<i>- Fly it.
- Yeah!</i>

11:53.578 --> 11:55.079
<i>- Toss it.
- Awesome.</i>

11:55.246 --> 11:56.747
<i>- Swim it.
- Aw.</i>

11:56.914 --> 11:58.332
<i>- Eat it.
- Whoa.</i>

11:58.499 --> 11:59.875
<i>Hasbro's Best Thing Ever.</i>

12:00.042 --> 12:03.838
<i>Kids! Kids! Aah! It's so awesome!</i>

12:04.006 --> 12:05.214
I want it.

12:09.677 --> 12:11.512
Hey, fellas. Um...

12:11.679 --> 12:13.472
I have a question.

12:13.639 --> 12:16.559
I went on a date
with this girl that I really like...

12:16.726 --> 12:21.147
...and if you don't mind, I was hoping
I could ask you a few questions...

12:21.314 --> 12:22.648
...about the birds and the bees.

12:22.815 --> 12:26.193
- Ah, my boy wants to know about sex.
- Came to the right place.

12:26.360 --> 12:30.031
Chris, what you always wanna remember
is that sex is perfectly natural.

12:30.197 --> 12:34.744
Well, uh, sorry, Mr. Swanson,
I wasn't really talking to you.

12:34.910 --> 12:37.038
Chris, I know a lot about sex.

12:37.204 --> 12:39.582
Yeah,
and I'm sure you have fond memories...

12:39.749 --> 12:41.500
...but I was hoping to get advice...

12:41.667 --> 12:44.212
...from someone who isn't broken
from the waist down.

12:44.378 --> 12:47.214
- I'm a father!
- You're a two-wheeled monster!

12:50.259 --> 12:53.555
That's gonna be my ringtone.
Quagmire, call me.

12:57.808 --> 12:59.185
Ha-ha-ha.

13:02.813 --> 13:06.525
I have to get to work, Chris.
I have tons of dogs to incinerate.

13:06.692 --> 13:09.028
But I can't wait to see you
tomorrow night.

13:09.195 --> 13:11.489
Oh, God. I'm so sorry.
I'll clean that up.

13:11.655 --> 13:14.492
Oh, that's okay. I'll get it.
Have fun at work.

13:14.658 --> 13:17.661
Okay. Bye, Chris.

13:17.829 --> 13:19.955
- What do you think you're doing?
- What?

13:20.122 --> 13:24.168
You, a man, are cleaning up a mess
made by Anna, a woman...

13:24.335 --> 13:25.961
...that she, also a woman...

13:26.128 --> 13:28.632
...spilled on you, a man.
- So?

13:28.799 --> 13:30.508
You're treating her like a human.

13:30.674 --> 13:34.011
If you wanna get anywhere with a chick,
you can't treat them nice-like.

13:34.178 --> 13:35.554
- Really?
- Trust me, Chris.

13:35.721 --> 13:38.141
Next time you see this girl,
treat her like crap.

13:38.308 --> 13:42.646
And you'll be cooler than a mid-'80s
novelty answering-machine message.

13:42.813 --> 13:44.897
<i>I'm glad you called, but I'm not home</i>

13:45.064 --> 13:46.565
<i>But I'll be back before too long</i>

13:46.732 --> 13:48.901
<i>Gotta wait for the beep
Gotta leave your name</i>

13:49.068 --> 13:50.820
<i>Gotta leave your number
Wait for the beep</i>

13:52.197 --> 13:54.907
<i>It's me again,
I just had to hear it one more time.</i>

13:57.494 --> 13:59.286
Chris, is everything okay?

13:59.453 --> 14:02.332
You seem a little,
I don't know, quiet tonight.

14:02.499 --> 14:03.958
Yeah, everything's fine.

14:04.125 --> 14:05.835
Yes, can I have two tickets?

14:06.001 --> 14:08.879
One man and one bitch
that needs to do what I say.

14:09.046 --> 14:11.841
- What? That's not funny, Chris.
- Here's your ticket.

14:12.008 --> 14:14.844
- Pick that up.
- Chris, why are you acting like this?

14:15.010 --> 14:17.556
Pick that up and cook it
into something delicious...

14:17.722 --> 14:19.723
...or knit it into something
that's useful to me.

14:24.395 --> 14:25.437
Um...

14:25.604 --> 14:27.065
Are you ready to make out now?

14:27.232 --> 14:30.401
Why in the world would I wanna do that
after what you just said?

14:30.568 --> 14:32.654
You're not the person
I thought you were.

14:32.821 --> 14:36.448
I never wanna see you again. I can't
believe I thought you were special.

14:37.033 --> 14:38.284
Anna, wait.

14:38.576 --> 14:40.995
Oh, no. What did I do?

14:41.161 --> 14:43.539
Chris, guess what we just did.
Bonnie, tell him.

14:43.706 --> 14:45.332
- We had sex.
- We had sex!

14:45.499 --> 14:47.752
We had what Joe calls sex.

14:53.883 --> 14:55.551
Chris, honey, what's wrong?

14:55.718 --> 14:58.178
- Anna took a dump on me.
- What?

14:58.345 --> 15:00.389
Yeah, she broke up with me.

15:00.556 --> 15:03.601
Oh, she dumped you.
That's what you meant to say.

15:04.351 --> 15:07.814
- What's the difference?
- Well, what you said first was what...

15:07.981 --> 15:11.902
Well, I mean, when two grownups
love each other very much...

15:12.068 --> 15:14.945
...sometimes they show it by...
Never mind.

15:15.112 --> 15:16.615
So, what happened?

15:16.781 --> 15:19.617
I don't know.
I did everything Dad said.

15:19.783 --> 15:22.412
I should've known
Peter had something to do with this.

15:22.579 --> 15:25.205
You're not the first person
whose life he's screwed up.

15:29.460 --> 15:34.006
Knock, knock.
Nicole, Ronald, who's ready for Boggle?

15:34.173 --> 15:35.967
Oh, my God. No!

15:36.134 --> 15:39.428
Why? Why? My beautiful Nicole.

15:39.595 --> 15:41.806
My man Ronald. Who did this?

15:41.973 --> 15:44.475
Oh, man, they were so good together.

15:44.642 --> 15:47.103
We were just establishing
our friendship.

15:47.270 --> 15:48.937
They were about to get engaged.

15:49.104 --> 15:51.524
Oh, he was gonna ask me
to be an usher.

15:51.691 --> 15:54.902
He already had enough groomsmen,
so he made me an usher...

15:55.069 --> 15:59.365
...but just to think I could be involved
in the ceremony in any way.

15:59.531 --> 16:02.077
You told Chris
to act like a jerk to this girl?

16:02.243 --> 16:06.623
- Well, define Chris.
- Peter, he's really upset right now.

16:06.790 --> 16:10.543
I mean, he cared about this girl a lot.
Can't you see what you've done?

16:10.710 --> 16:12.961
I don't know.
I mean, I thought I was helping.

16:13.128 --> 16:14.254
But you may be right...

16:14.421 --> 16:17.925
...because now Chris is all sad
and crying and fat and bad at sports.

16:18.092 --> 16:21.221
Well, you created this mess,
and you have to help him fix it.

16:21.388 --> 16:25.642
Man, parenting is more complicated
than making a 1940s phone call.

16:26.059 --> 16:28.811
Hello, operator?
Crestview 4162, please.

16:28.977 --> 16:30.313
<i>One moment, please.</i>

16:47.413 --> 16:48.455
- Hello.
- Hello?

16:48.622 --> 16:50.458
- Hello? Hello?
- Hello? Hello?

16:50.625 --> 16:52.043
Hello?

16:52.209 --> 16:54.420
Well, what do you know about that?

17:02.678 --> 17:06.182
Hey, Chris, it's me.
I got something for you here.

17:06.349 --> 17:09.018
- What is it?
- I caught you a bullfrog outside.

17:09.185 --> 17:11.646
Poked some holes in its back
so it can breathe.

17:11.813 --> 17:14.440
See, look at this... Oh, boy.

17:14.607 --> 17:16.734
All right, hang on, hang on.

17:57.816 --> 17:59.986
I'm never gonna be happy again.

18:00.153 --> 18:02.529
I know how you feel, son,
but you can't give up.

18:02.696 --> 18:04.741
Let's get out there
and meet some ladies.

18:04.908 --> 18:08.286
But I don't wanna date anyone else.
I want Anna.

18:08.453 --> 18:11.580
Chris, you don't wanna miss out
experiencing your teenage years.

18:11.747 --> 18:14.584
You'll feel as bad as I do
when I miss the toilet.

18:18.296 --> 18:20.131
Peter Griffin!

18:26.179 --> 18:28.598
Have a seat.
Your date will be here any minute.

18:28.765 --> 18:32.644
In fact, I think she'll be coming
through that door.

18:33.144 --> 18:36.105
Hey, Chris, I'm Betty. Sorry I'm late.

18:36.271 --> 18:39.984
Your dad told me all about you.
You sound like a swell fella.

18:40.151 --> 18:43.738
Uh, thanks. So where are you from?

18:43.905 --> 18:46.823
I'm from the rich part of town,
so you know I'm a good egg.

18:46.990 --> 18:48.743
But I'm more interested in you.

18:48.910 --> 18:51.411
- Did you finish your homework today?
- What?

18:51.578 --> 18:53.831
You know,
your dad's got a birthday coming up.

18:53.998 --> 18:56.500
Given any thought
to what you might be getting him?

18:56.667 --> 18:58.795
How do you know
when my dad's birthday is?

18:58.961 --> 19:02.840
Well... It doesn't matter. What are you
getting your dad for his birthday?

19:03.007 --> 19:04.842
I don't know. A tie.

19:05.009 --> 19:07.970
Oh, I don't know
if he would want one of those.

19:08.137 --> 19:09.639
I think he's got enough ties.

19:09.806 --> 19:10.848
He might...

19:11.014 --> 19:12.975
I don't want a tie. Pick something else.

19:14.644 --> 19:15.977
Chris, this is Barbara.

19:16.144 --> 19:18.523
The girl you used to have a crush on.

19:18.690 --> 19:21.650
You kids enjoy yourselves,
and I'll create some atmosphere.

19:21.818 --> 19:24.112
This is a favorite by Men at Work.

19:24.278 --> 19:27.156
<i>Do you come
From a land down under?</i>

19:27.865 --> 19:30.660
<i>Do you hear the thunder?</i>

19:31.243 --> 19:33.955
<i>Of a land down under</i>

19:34.414 --> 19:37.208
<i>Look at me
With a brand-new Hyundai</i>

19:40.378 --> 19:43.131
I don't understand,
your blind date should be here now.

19:43.297 --> 19:45.091
She answered the ad.

19:45.258 --> 19:46.884
Whoa.

19:51.764 --> 19:54.434
So still no luck on the girlfriend, huh?

19:54.600 --> 19:57.770
I know Dad's been trying to help.
I'm trying to listen to him...

19:57.937 --> 19:59.897
...but nothing seems to be working.

20:00.064 --> 20:01.607
I know I asked him to help...

20:01.774 --> 20:04.986
...but it occurs to me you've
been taking advice from everyone...

20:05.153 --> 20:07.321
...except the one person
who matters.

20:07.488 --> 20:08.906
What do you want, Chris?

20:09.073 --> 20:11.534
All I want
is to go out with Anna again.

20:11.701 --> 20:16.164
Then you just need to go talk to her
and tell her exactly how you feel.

20:16.330 --> 20:18.875
But she said
she never wants to see me again.

20:19.041 --> 20:22.503
Well, I'm sure you can come up
with some excuse to see her at the vet.

20:22.670 --> 20:24.589
Is there any more coffee?

20:27.216 --> 20:30.261
Anna, I'm here with my dog.

20:30.427 --> 20:31.929
He's not feeling well.

20:32.096 --> 20:33.514
Fuck you.

20:33.681 --> 20:35.641
Don't you think
you'd rather go to another vet?

20:35.808 --> 20:37.310
Anna, to be honest.

20:37.476 --> 20:39.645
I came here
because I wanted to apologize...

20:39.812 --> 20:41.480
...for acting like such a jerk.

20:41.647 --> 20:43.941
- That's not who I am.
- Oh, yeah. No, no.

20:44.108 --> 20:47.612
- No, yeah, no, you're a cool guy.
- Brian, shut up!

20:47.778 --> 20:51.741
I was just really nervous because
I've never had a girlfriend before...

20:51.908 --> 20:54.577
...and I wanted to make sure
I didn't do anything wrong.

20:54.744 --> 20:57.580
You know, you really hurt me, Chris.

20:57.747 --> 21:02.084
I know, I was wrong.
I don't wanna hurt anybody, Anna.

21:02.251 --> 21:04.629
Please, just give me another chance.

21:04.795 --> 21:08.466
- Gosh, he doesn't look so good.
- I know.

21:08.633 --> 21:10.760
But you do.

21:13.930 --> 21:16.599
You know, I get off at 4.

21:16.766 --> 21:19.644
I might just be up for a movie.

21:22.355 --> 21:25.441
Okay, somebody really needs
to help me here.

21:25.442 --> 22:26.442
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru